---
description: JStack per-role model choices (overrides skill defaults)
alwaysApply: true
---
# JStack model configuration, read by j-mode and the skills. One line per role. A comma in a role name means those roles share the line.
# Every role has a line. Any spawn without its own role uses `other helpers`. Never fall back to a model this file doesn't name.
# James Woods's choices: Anthropic leads every role and no OpenAI models are used. Gemini only takes a second seat on a panel an Anthropic agent leads.
# Use each level as written. Raise one step only for the hardest or subtlest work. Never start an Anthropic model on max, though escalating to max is fine.
# Load-bearing means hard to undo: data models and storage, public APIs, cross-service boundaries, and security.

# Jobs (see j-mode).
# Opus High: the Project chat routes work and briefs James. Cursor's Project settings set it; this line records it.
coordinator: claude-opus-5-5-high
# Opus High: an ordinary design is cheap to change later, so Extra High adds little.
architect: claude-opus-5-5-high
# Opus Extra High: a load-bearing design is hard to undo, so deeper reasoning changes the outcome.
architect for load-bearing designs: claude-opus-5-5-xhigh
# Opus High: an ordinary plan review checks order, gaps and risk lines.
plan reviewer: claude-opus-5-5-high
# Opus Extra High: on a load-bearing plan, its verdict gates every builder that follows.
plan reviewer for load-bearing plans: claude-opus-5-5-xhigh
# Builders start on Opus 5.5 Medium. Switch to the matching line below for a very complex change, very well-planned work, or a simple change with some ambiguity.
# Opus Medium: James's default builder (27 Oct). The plan and the reviewer carry the judgment.
builder: claude-opus-5-5-medium
# Opus High: a very complex change needs more reasoning than the default builder.
builder for a very complex change: claude-opus-5-5-high
builder for very well-planned work: claude-sonnet-5-5-high
builder for a simple change with some ambiguity: claude-sonnet-5-5-xhigh
# Opus Extra High: the hardest pieces (subtle concurrency, tricky algorithms, a bug two fixes have failed to kill) are where deeper reasoning changes the outcome.
hardest tasks: claude-opus-5-5-xhigh
# Opus High: one fresh holistic review per small or medium PR. High ties Extra High on CursorBench at about half the cost.
reviewer: claude-opus-5-5-high
investigator: claude-sonnet-5-5-high
watcher: claude-sonnet-5-5-medium
# Opus High: prose and judgment calls inside a job.
judgment and prose: claude-opus-5-5-high
# Opus High: the architecture and evidence lenses on a big change. The correctness lens uses `interrogate reviewers`.
lens reviewers: claude-opus-5-5-high
# Opus Extra High: its verdict gates merging a milestone, like the arena judge.
milestone reviewer: claude-opus-5-5-xhigh

# Skills.
how explorer: claude-sonnet-5-5-xhigh
# Opus High: explains what the explorers already traced, with the code at hand.
how explainer: claude-opus-5-5-high
why investigators: claude-sonnet-5-5-xhigh
# Opus High: careful synthesis, but its answer informs James and gates nothing.
why synthesizer: claude-opus-5-5-high
reflect tooling: claude-sonnet-5-5-xhigh
# Opus High: James approves every proposed skill edit, so these seats don't make the final call.
reflect judgment, divergent, synthesizer: claude-opus-5-5-high
# Opus High: runners only produce candidates for the parent to pick from.
arena runners: claude-opus-5-5-high, gemini-4-argon-high
# Opus Extra High: the judge's verdict picks the base that later work builds on.
arena cross-judge pool: claude-opus-5-5-xhigh
swarm workers: claude-sonnet-5-5-high
# Opus High: runners produce candidate designs; the architect makes the call.
architect runners: claude-opus-5-5-high, gemini-4-argon-high
# Opus Extra High: /interrogate runs on big changes, where a missed bug is costly.
interrogate reviewers: claude-opus-5-5-xhigh, gemini-4-argon-high
# Opus High: scans a decision trail for weak evidence and flags it. The flags are advice.
trail reviewer: claude-opus-5-5-high
comment sicko: claude-sonnet-5-5-high
other helpers: claude-sonnet-5-5-high
